#### Article 27

1. Improvement of accessibility and expansion of services as referred to in Article 24 letter c shall be carried out through:  
a. provision of child and adolescent friendly, gender responsive and inclusive access and services before violence against children occurs, and  
b. provision of child and adolescent friendly, gender responsive and inclusive access and services after violence against children occurs.  
2. Improvement of accessibility and expansion of services through provision of child and adolescent friendly, gender responsive and inclusive access and services before violence against children occurs as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a, shall be carried out through regional government policy intervention towards:  
a. provision of child friendly information services;  
b. developing Adolescent Posyandu services starting from the hamlet/neighborhood level, and  
c. optimization of services to reduce vulnerability in children.  
3. Improvement of accessibility and expansion of services through provision of child and adolescent friendly, gender responsive and inclusive access and services after violence against children occurs as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, shall be carried out through regional government policy intervention towards:  
a. Development of a comprehensive service referral system for vulnerable children, and  
b. Assistance for children requiring special Protection to obtain their rights as children.  
4. Improvement of accessibility and expansion of services may be carried out by strengthening existing service institutions, namely:  
a. community health centers;  
b. posyandu, Adolescent Posyandu and Family Posyandu;  
c. UPTD PPA;  
d. Family Learning Center (PUSPAGA);  
e. Family Welfare Consultation Institution (LK3);  
f. Child Protection Organizing Institution;  
g. Prosperous Family Service Center (PPKS), and  
h. Child Social Welfare Institution (LKSA).

#### Article 28

Strengthening of regulations and institutions as referred to (1) in Article 24 letter d shall be carried out through:  
a. strengthening institutional capacity for child Protection and empowerment and education units,  
b. encouraging the establishment of village regulations and village head regulations concerning child Protection,  
c. conducting evaluations of village regulations, school regulations and/or awiq-awiq that encourage violence and vulnerability in children, and  
2. Strengthening institutional capacity for child Protection and empowerment and education units as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a shall be carried out through regional government policy intervention towards increasing knowledge and skills of law enforcement officers, village apparatus, KUA officers, customary stakeholders, extension workers and teachers.

#### Article 29

1. Strengthening coordination of stakeholders as referred to in Article 24 letter e shall be carried out through strategies focused on:  
a. improving cross-sectoral, cross-field, and cross-regional cooperation;  
b. strengthening data and information systems, and  
c. supervision, monitoring, and evaluation.  
2. Strengthening coordination of stakeholders as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out through regional government policy intervention towards:  
a. strengthening coordination forums for planning and implementation of child Protection policies,  
b. utilization of data for policy improvement, and  
c. building data and information systems as a basis for implementing referral services for children requiring special Protection.

## Part Three

Handling

#### Article 30

1. Handling as referred to in Article 23 letter b, includes:  
a. rehabilitation services, covering physical, medical, psychological, educational, and social rehabilitation;  
b. facilitation of legal aid services;  
c. facilitation of fulfillment of basic needs, covering food, clothing, housing, education, health, learning and recreation, security guarantees, and equal treatment;  
d. facilitation of fulfillment of special needs for children with disabilities and psychosocial disorders;  
e. facilitation of health services;  
f. repatriation and social reintegration, and  
g. protection of child witnesses.  
2. Protection of child witnesses as referred to in paragraph (1) letter g, shall be implemented through:  
a. facilitation of medical, psychological rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, within institutions and outside institutions;  
b. facilitation of safety guarantees; and  
c. facilitation of ease in obtaining information regarding case developments.

#### Article 31

In order to carry out handling in the effort of Special Protection for Children, the Regional Government needs to provide a child social protection house/comprehensive integrated child safe house.

# CHAPTER VI

## COORDINATION TEAM FOR PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

#### Article 32

1. The Regent shall establish a Coordination Team for Protection of Women and Children.  
2. The Coordination Team for Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1), serves as a coordination forum in implementing empowerment, Protection of women, fulfillment of Children's Rights and Special Protection for Children in the region, which has functions including:  
a. facilitation in empowerment and Protection of women, and  
b. facilitation in efforts to fulfill Children's Rights and Special Protection for Children.  
3. Membership of the Coordination Team for Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), shall consist of at least:  
a. elements of Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child Protection;  
b. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of education;  
c. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of health;  
d. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of social affairs;  
e. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of transportation;  
f. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of community and village empowerment;  
g. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of population and civil registration;  
h. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of communication and informatics;  
i. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of manpower and transmigration;  
j. Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of highways and spatial planning;  
k. elements of the Police;  
l. elements of the Prosecutor's Office;  
m. elements of the Court;  
n. elements of the Children's Forum;  
o. educational institutions;  
p. community organizations concerned with Protection of women and children;  
q. media, and  
r. community.  
4. The Coordination Team for Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), shall be established by Regent's Decree.

# CHAPTER VII

## INSTITUTIONS

#### Article 33

1. The regional government shall establish UPTD PPA which carries out Handling, Protection, and Recovery of Victims, Victims' Families, and/or Witnesses.  
2. UPTD PPA shall be positioned in the work unit implementing governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.  
3. Establishment of UPTD PPA shall be stipulated by Regent's Regulation after meeting requirements in accordance with statutory provisions.  
4. UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall have the duties to:  
a. receive reports or outreach to Victims;  
b. provide information about Victims' rights;  
c. facilitate provision of health services;  
d. facilitate provision of psychological strengthening services;  
e. facilitate provision of psychosocial services, social rehabilitation, social empowerment, and social reintegration;  
f. provide legal services;  
g. identify economic empowerment needs;  
h. identify temporary shelter needs for Victims and Victims' Families that need to be fulfilled immediately;  
i. facilitate needs of Victims with Disabilities;  
j. coordinate and work together on fulfillment of Victims' rights with other institutions, and  
k. monitor fulfillment of Victims' rights by law enforcement apparatus during the judicial process.
